From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:45:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] Linux: an id of the install's own where the disks give
 none

The serial number Linden Lab's login and stats see (id0) is the MD5 of the
longest name in /dev/disk/by-uuid. A container has no such folder, so every
container install sent the MD5 of nothing, the same id, tying all their
accounts together. Where there's no disk id, the viewer now uses one of the
install's own: a random UUID made the first time and kept in the viewer's
settings folder (install_id), so it lasts as long as the saved login does.
---
 doc/IBASHO-CHANGES.txt             |  4 +++
 indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/IBASHO-CHANGES.txt b/doc/IBASHO-CHANGES.txt
index 9548dbe..d59ca6c 100644
--- a/doc/IBASHO-CHANGES.txt
+++ b/doc/IBASHO-CHANGES.txt
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@ indra/newview/llappviewer.cpp
     frame rate cap (IbashoMaxFPS, IbashoIdleFPS).
 indra/newview/llappviewer.h
     Modified for Ibasho (2026-10-22): the window class is Ibasho's own.
+indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp
+    Modified for Ibasho (2026-11-03): where the disks give no id (a container), the serial number is
+    made from an id of the install's own, kept in the viewer's settings folder, instead of from
+    nothing.
 indra/newview/llappviewerwin32.cpp
     Modified for Ibasho (2026-10-22): the single-instance mutex is Ibasho's own.
 indra/newview/llavatarpropertiesprocessor.cpp
diff --git a/indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp b/indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp
index 2fd0eeb..0f48d8d 100644
--- a/indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp
+++ b/indra/newview/llappviewerlinux.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,10 @@
  *
  * Linden Research, Inc., 945 Battery Street, San Francisco, CA  94111  USA
  * $/LicenseInfo$
+ *
+ * Modified for Ibasho (2026-11-03): where the disks give no id (a container has no /dev/disk/by-uuid), the
+ * serial number is made from an id of this install's own instead of from nothing, which every such install
